From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: the UFS root device, and the console log that rides on it

MILANF has had no block device at all. bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c is 'standard' in
bsd/conf/files, so it compiles on every board, but its whole body sits inside
#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) and milanf has been getting an empty
translation unit. No UFS, no GPT scan, no disk, and rd=ufsroot0 resolving to
nothing. This is the patch that gives the board a filesystem.

It is the one to enable first because it carries no board constants worth
arguing about: zero hardcoded addresses. It looks up /sweet-ufs in the ADT and
drives whatever base it finds there; the milanf ADT publishes that node at
0x04804000, the ufshc block in the unit's own device tree, and the bootloader
left the link up because it loaded us over it. The rest of the driver is
UFSHCI 2.1 register offsets and SCSI command construction, which are the same
on any Qualcomm UFS host.

Three things had to move with it, and the reason is the same for all three:
the symbol lives in sweet_ufs.c, but its caller is outside the guard.

  - iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp gates the rd=ufsroot0 branch on
    ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET. Without widening it the driver would have
    compiled and been unreachable, and rd=ufsroot0 would have fallen through
    to the generic root-device path.

  - osfmk/console/serial_console.c calls sweet_log_append() from _cnputs under
    the same guard, which is the persistent 4 MB console ring that
    tools/sweet-log-pull.sh reads back off the partition. On a board with no
    serial port that log is the only post-mortem there is, so it comes in with
    the driver that implements it. sweet_log_append() itself is a bare ring
    buffer write with no hardware access and no lock, safe from any context,
    including before the UFS driver has initialised - which is the case for
    every line printed during early boot.

  - sweet_ufs_init() calls sweet_keys_init(), sweet_touch_init() and
    sweet_usb_probe(). Those three are NOT being enabled: the SPMI blocks,
    the touch controller at 0x00a84000 (which on milanf lands inside the
    blair-pinctrl block) and the DWC3 controller at 0x0a600000 do not exist at
    sweet's addresses on this SoC. Each gets an #elif
    defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF) arm that supplies an empty entry point,
    so the boot sequence stays a plain sequence of calls and each driver
    states its own board support status in its own file. They become real
    drivers - and lose their stub - when their values are read off this unit's
    DTB.

Checked before writing this: for each of those three files, the only symbol
referenced from outside its own file is that init entry point (every other
definition in them is file-local), so the stub is exactly the link surface
required and nothing else is left dangling.

The IOLog/printf strings keep their SWEET: prefix, same as 0088 and for the
same reason: the pull and symbolication tooling greps for them.

Verified without a compiler: bash-side checks are meaningless here, so this
was diffed against the tree and then applied for real to a scratch copy in
series order after 0086/0087/0088 (none of which touch these six files), with
core.autocrlf=false, producing CR=0 results throughout. The link is still
unverified - that needs CI.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c
index a148608..88132f3 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_keys.c
@@ -179,4 +179,16 @@ sweet_keys_init(void)
 		printf("SWEET KEYS: kernel_thread_start failed %d\n", kr);
 	}
 }
+#elif defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
+/*
+ * Not started on milanf yet: this driver reads the SPMI observation and
+ * config blocks at sweet's addresses (0x0e600000, 0x0c40a000), and the PMIC
+ * arbiter on this SoC answers at a different base - 0x1c40000, per
+ * /soc/qcom,spmi@1c40000 in the unit's own device tree. The entry point
+ * exists so the boot sequence in sweet_ufs.c can call it unconditionally.
+ */
+void
+sweet_keys_init(void)
+{
+}
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
index 03defe6..fbdfdf9 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -657,4 +657,16 @@ sweet_touch_init(void)
 		printf("SWEET TOUCH: kernel_thread_start failed %d\n", kr);
 	}
 }
+#elif defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
+/*
+ * Not started on milanf yet: sweet's touch controller address, 0x00a84000,
+ * lands inside this SoC's pinctrl block, and the I2C and TLMM bases the
+ * driver uses do not exist here either. Zero of its three addresses survive
+ * the jump. The entry point exists so the boot sequence in sweet_ufs.c can
+ * call it unconditionally.
+ */
+void
+sweet_touch_init(void)
+{
+}
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
index 6b926fe..7f59a79 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
  * against the partition bounds again right before it is issued, so nothing
  * outside the named partition can be written.
  */
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 #include <sys/param.h>
 #include <sys/systm.h>
 #include <sys/buf.h>
@@ -820,4 +820,4 @@ sweet_ufs_rootdev(dev_t *dev)
 	*dev = su.bdev;
 	return 0;
 }
-#endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
+#endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET || ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF */
diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
index b6c1a41..32c571c 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
@@ -928,4 +928,15 @@ sweet_usb_gadget_start(vm_offset_t dwc)
 		thread_deallocate(thread);
 	}
 }
+#elif defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
+/*
+ * Not started on milanf yet: the DWC3 controller is not at sweet's base
+ * (0x0a600000), and neither the QMP PHY block nor the USB3 wrapper address
+ * this driver uses exists on this SoC. The entry point exists so the boot
+ * sequence in sweet_ufs.c can call it unconditionally.
+ */
+void
+sweet_usb_probe(void)
+{
+}
 #endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET */
diff --git a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
index e6c74aa..1d43239 100644
--- a/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp
@@ -766,7 +766,7 @@ IOFindBSDRoot( char * rootName, unsigned int rootNameSize,
 		}
 	}
 
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 //
 //	SWEET: root on a GPT partition of the internal UFS (bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c)
 //
@@ -782,7 +782,7 @@ IOFindBSDRoot( char * rootName, unsigned int rootNameSize,
 		*oflags = 0;
 		goto iofrootx;
 	}
-#endif
+#endif /* ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET || ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF */
 
 //
 //	Now check if we are trying to root on a memory device
diff --git a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
index c86b9e7..45a69dc 100644
--- a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
@@ -266,7 +266,7 @@ _cnputc(char c, bool poll)
  *             waiting for an interrupt when the hardware device isn't ready
  * @param size The number of characters to print to the console.
  */
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 extern void sweet_log_append(const char *c, int size);  /* bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c */
 /*
  * Set by AppleCLCD (boot-arg sweetfb_noconsole=1) once the GUI presents:
@@ -281,7 +281,7 @@ _cnputs(char *c, int size, bool poll)
 {
 	extern int disableConsoleOutput;
 
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 	sweet_log_append(c, size);
 	if (sweet_console_muted && !panic_active()) {
 		return;
